    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Low-traffic verification — cumulative counters",
      "description": "Additional panels use raw exported counters for short demonstrations, alongside the existing rate/increase panels.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**M4.3D3 — Low-traffic verification.** The charts below show raw cumulative counters from the currently exporting processes. They are easier to inspect after just a few synthetic registrations than `rate()` / `increase()` charts. **Not lifetime business totals:** counters may reset on process restart and can include retries. The SQL databases are authoritative. `No data` is not the same as zero."
      }
